{"type":"step-attempt","step":"cross-boundary-invariants","sessionId":"ed305204-939e-4e3f-90d7-392dae4080a6","outcome":{"verdict":"escalation","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/step-timeout-last-progress/cross-boundary-invariants-result-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"approved":false,"findings":[{"severity":"medium","resolution":"decision-needed","file":"src/adapter/shared/last-tool-tracker.ts","title":"onToolEnd(undefined) best-effort match silently clears any in-flight tool","rationale":"The isToolResult guard types tool_use_id as optional (defensive coding), so firstResult?.tool_use_id can be undefined. When onToolEnd(undefined) is called, the condition `id === undefined` satisfies `correlates` for ANY tracked in-flight tool regardless of its id. A tool_result-shaped user message without tool_use_id (synthetic stream, legacy format, or future SDK message type that incidentally passes isToolResult) would incorrectly mark the in-flight tool as 'done', causing timeoutHint() to report 'completed before timeout' even if the tool was still running.","line":46,"options":[{"label":"Accept as-is: real SDK always provides tool_use_id, ponytail comment documents the ceiling","consequence":"Low production risk (real SDK tool_result blocks always carry tool_use_id: string). Synthetic/legacy streams may get incorrect 'completed' hints. The existing ponytail comment covers this."},{"label":"Guard: only call onToolEnd when tool_use_id is defined","consequence":"Eliminates false-positive completion signals at the cost of leaving any tool with a missing id permanently in-flight in timeoutHint. Safer for diagnostic accuracy."}]},{"severity":"low","resolution":"decision-needed","file":"src/adapter/claude-code/agent-runner.ts","title":"tracker state not reset between transient retry attempts","rationale":"When maxRetries > 0 and a transient error occurs, retryWithBackoff retries runMainWorkTurn. The tracker is not reset between retries. If attempt 1 observed a tool_use (startedAt = T0) and then failed transiently, attempt 2's timeoutHint() reports that tool with elapsed = now() - T0, which includes the retry delay. An operator reading the hint would see an implausibly large elapsed time for the tool.","line":843,"options":[{"label":"Accept as-is: transient retry + STEP_TIMEOUT is a rare compound condition","consequence":"Misleading elapsed time in the niche case of transient-retry-then-timeout. Tool name is still correct. Risk is low given maxRetries>0 is non-default config."},{"label":"Reset tracker at the start of each runMainWorkTurn retry iteration","consequence":"Accurate elapsed time per attempt. Requires passing or resetting the tracker between retries inside runMainWorkTurn."}]},{"severity":"low","resolution":"decision-needed","file":"src/adapter/claude-code/agent-runner.ts","title":"isToolResult matches SDKUserMessageReplay in resumed sessions","rationale":"SDKUserMessageReplay has type='user' and is not distinguished by isToolResult from SDKUserMessage. In resumed sessions the SDK may replay prior-session tool_result messages, calling tracker.onToolEnd for old tool_use_ids. In the narrow window between replay completion and the first new tool_use of the current session, a timeout would show a completed prior-session tool rather than a current-session tool.","line":492,"options":[{"label":"Accept as-is: replayed tools are completed, hint is technically accurate for the replayed tool","consequence":"Slightly confusing if the operator expects the hint to reflect the current session only. In practice, the resumed session quickly emits new tool_use events, minimizing the window."},{"label":"Reset tracker at session resume boundary (when resumeSessionId is used)","consequence":"Tracker starts fresh per actual SDK session. Requires detecting the replay/live boundary, which the SDK does not expose explicitly."}]}],"evidence":{"checked":18,"skipped":0,"unverified":0},"observations":[{"severity":"low","file":"src/adapter/claude-code/agent-runner.ts","title":"isToolUse called twice per tool_use message","rationale":"observeMessage calls emitToolProgress (which calls isToolUse internally) then calls isToolUse again in the closure body. Harmless (pure function) but redundant.","line":493},{"severity":"low","file":"src/adapter/shared/last-tool-tracker.ts","title":"elapsed measured at catch-block entry, not at watchdog fire time","rationale":"The gap between watchdog.abort() and the catch block executing timeoutHint() is sub-millisecond in production and zero under vitest fake timers. Design explicitly acknowledges this in the Risks section.","line":54},{"severity":"low","file":"src/adapter/claude-code/agent-runner.ts","title":"reportRetry follow-up path does not pass observeMessage","rationale":"Pre-existing behavior: bare emitToolProgress was not called on the reportRetry path before the diff either. Per design D3 only the three explicitly listed sites are wired (main, postWork, output-repair). Not a regression.","line":937},{"severity":"low","file":"src/adapter/shared/__tests__/last-tool-tracker.test.ts","title":"All 6 AC-#5 test files and full suite green","rationale":"bun run typecheck && bun run test: 768 test files, 11469 tests passed, 1 skipped. All 6 invariant test files (inactivity-watchdog, executor-sequential-regression, commit-orchestrator, executor-drift-detection, no-op-detect-exemption, agent-runner-transient-retry) have zero diff from main and are green."}]},"followUpAttempts":0,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":0}},"startedAt":"2026-08-14T16:47:04.876Z","endedAt":"2026-08-14T17:02:12.845Z"}
